Loom AIE2P / XDNA: the compiler pieces of the engine's NPU cascade GEMM: memory-tile staging, replay and multicast,
shared panels, cascade link timing, worker.accumulate, leaf-synchronized channels (constrain.leaf_sync), re-armed
replay rings for the control-only continuation, LOOM_EXP_* placement and packing knobs. NPU-only code paths.
Grouped / streamed shared panels (LOOM_EXP_PANEL_GROUPS, LOOM_EXP_PANEL_STREAM): a panel slice
replays in groups of records, counting locks let a group refill with the next invocation's data while the other group
replays, the control program becomes [even push | waits | odd push] (parity shim descriptor sets, paced fills retired by
their completion tokens) and the product publishes four invocations (setup + even push + waits, even push, odd push,
waits); unstreamed products are unchanged.

